-- title:
--   Existence of a moduli place for the Frobenius-twisted Γ₀(M')-class
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $q$, an integer $M'\neq 0$ with $q\nmid M'$, and a prime $\ell_g$ with $\ell_g\equiv 11 \pmod{12}$ and $\ell_g\mid M'$.
--
--   **The global valuation ring and the reduction datum.** Let $A$ be a valuation subring of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ with `A.LiesOverPrime q`, i.e. $q$ is a non-unit of $A$; consequently the residue field $\kappa(A)$ has characteristic $q$ (via [`ValuationSubring.charP_residueField_of_liesOverPrime_def`](def/WeierstrassCurve_ReductionMap.html#L57)). Let $W$ be a finite set of places of `modularFunctionFieldC (ResidueField A) M'` over $\kappa(A)$ (the intermediate field of $\kappa(A)((t))$ generated by `jqModC` and its $q$-stretch `jqNModC … q`), and let `hW` say that $W$ consists exactly of the members of `ssPlaces q M' (ResidueField A)`, that is, of the places $w$ that are rational (the structure map $\kappa(A)\to\kappa(w)$ is surjective), satisfy the predicate `IsAffineGeomPlace`, and have $w$-value of `jGeomGen (ResidueField A) M'` lying in the set `ssJSet q`. The hypothesis `hle` asserts the inclusion `modularFunctionFieldBar M' ≤ fieldBar q M'` of intermediate fields of $\overline{\mathbb Q}((t))$, the former being the base change to $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ of the full level-$M'$ modular function field, the latter the base change of the function field of $X_H(q^2M')$ for $H=$ `levelH q M'`. Let $R_0$ be a `ConstantReduction` of `modularFunctionFieldBar M'` to `modularFunctionFieldC (ResidueField A) M'` over $A$: a valuation subring $R_0.\mathrm{integers}$, a surjective residue homomorphism onto the target with kernel the maximal ideal, a map on places preserving degrees, and the compatibilities with $A$ and with orders of elements recorded in that structure. The hypothesis `hR₀` requires that for every Laurent series $y$ with coefficients in $A$ whose coefficientwise image in $\overline{\mathbb Q}((t))$ lies in `modularFunctionFieldBar M'`, that image is $R_0$-integral and its $R_0$-residue is the coefficientwise reduction of $y$ modulo the maximal ideal of $A$. Finally $s$ is an element of $W$.
--
--   **The small field of constants.** Let $k_0$ be an intermediate field of $\overline{\mathbb Q}/\mathbb Q$ and write $A_0$ for `A.comap (algebraMap ↥k₀ (AlgebraicClosure ℚ))`, the valuation subring of $k_0$ induced by $A$. Let $\pi_0\in k_0$ have image in $A$ (`hπ`). The hypotheses `hdvr`, `hunif`, `hhens`, `hres` require that $A_0$ be a discrete valuation ring, that its maximal ideal be generated by $\pi_0$, that it be henselian, and that its residue field be algebraically closed; `hκ` requires that every $a\in A$ be congruent, modulo the maximal ideal of $A$, to an element of $k_0$ lying in $A$.
--
--   **Roots of unity, level and function field.** Let $\xi\in k_0$ be a primitive $(q\ell_g)$-th root of unity (`hξ`), and `hιξ` require a ring homomorphism $\iota:k_0\to\mathbb C$ with $\iota(\xi)=\exp(2\pi i/(q\ell_g))$. Let $H_1\le (\mathbb Z/q^2M')^\times$ be, by `hH₁`, the intersection of `levelH q M'` (the kernel of reduction to $(\mathbb Z/q)^\times$) with the kernel of reduction to $(\mathbb Z/\ell_g)^\times$. Let $K$ be an intermediate field of $k_0((t))/k_0$ which by `hK` equals `laurentBaseChange ↥k₀ (xHFunctionField (q ^ 2 * M') H₁)`, the base change to $k_0$ of the function field of $X_{H_1}(q^2M')$, equipped with an $A_0$-algebra structure making $A_0\to k_0\to K$ a scalar tower. Let $j\in K$ have Laurent expansion `coeffEmb ↥k₀ jq`, with $j\neq 0$.
--
--   **Equivariance hypotheses for the level structures.** `hℓ` asserts that for every $A_0$-algebra $T$, every Weierstrass curve $W$ over $T$, every variable change $C$ and every `LevelPData` $D$, if $D$ is a $\Gamma_1(\ell_g)$-point of $W$ (i.e. $(x_P,y_P)$ satisfies the affine equation, $\mathrm{pre}\Psi_{\ell_g}(x_P)=0$, and $(x_Q,y_Q)=(x_P,y_P)$) then the transformed data is a $\Gamma_1(\ell_g)$-point of $C\cdot W$. `hM` asserts the corresponding statement for `IsGamma0PowAt W p k h` and the transform `kernelVariableChangeDeg C (gamma0PowDeg p k) h`. `hL` asserts that a divisor $h$ of `inLineMulPoly W ℓg n x` transforms, under `kernelVariableChangeDeg C d`, into a divisor of `inLineMulPoly (C • W) ℓg n (u^{-2}(x-r))`. Let $\mathcal G$ be a family `GroupLaws A₀` of relative group laws on the projective models of Weierstrass curves with unit discriminant, assumed chord-and-tangent (`h𝒢`) and with identity section at the origin chart (`h𝒢O`), and let $\mathcal T$ be a `LevelTransport A₀ 𝒢 q` of raw Drinfeld pairs, assumed a section transport (`h𝒯`), so that its action and functoriality are implemented by the expected morphisms of projective models. The hypotheses `hVC` and `hCO` require, for every $A_0$-algebra $T$ and every projective Weierstrass curve over $T$, the existence of graded ring homomorphisms realising a variable change, respectively a coefficient change along an $A_0$-algebra map, on the graded quotient rings attached to the projective models, each carrying the irrelevant ideal of the target into the image of the irrelevant ideal of the source, and satisfying `IsVariableChangeHom`, respectively `IsCoefficientHom`.
--
--   Write $\mathcal R$ for `rigidDataH1Pow A₀ ℓg M' q hℓ hM hL 𝒢 𝒯`: the rigid Weierstrass data whose raw objects over an $A_0$-algebra $T$ consist of a Weierstrass curve with unit discriminant together with a triple, namely a family of $\Gamma_0(p^{v_p(M')})$-kernel polynomials indexed by the prime factors $p$ of $M'$, a `LevelPData` which is a $\Gamma_1(\ell_g)$-point, and a raw Drinfeld pair forming a Drinfeld basis of level $q$ for $\mathcal G$, subject to the link condition `IsGamma1Link` that the kernel polynomial at $\ell_g$ divides `inLineMulPoly` at the $\Gamma_1$-point; its points $\mathcal R.\mathrm{Pt}(T)$ are the raw objects modulo variable change.
--
--   **The moduli package and the Tate pin.** Let $P_0$ be a `LevelModuliPackageAbs` for $\mathcal R$'s moduli datum: an $A_0$-algebra $B_0$ with a universal point `P₀.univ` such that every point over every $A_0$-algebra is the image of `P₀.univ` under a unique $A_0$-algebra homomorphism. Let $x_0\in \mathcal R.\mathrm{Pt}(K)$ satisfy `hx₀`: its $j$-invariant has Laurent expansion `jqNModC ↥k₀ q`. Let `clC` be an $A_0$-algebra homomorphism from $B_0$ to the chart algebra `TwoChartIntegralModel.chartAlgFin A₀ K j` (the elements of $K$ integral over $A_0[j]$), with `hclC` saying that `clC` followed by the inclusion into $K$ is the classifying map $P_0.\mathrm{classify}\,x_0$.
--
--   The hypothesis `hμ` pins $x_0$ at the Tate curve. It requires a variable change $C$ over $k_0((t))$ and a raw datum $r$ over $K$ whose class is $x_0$, such that: (i) with $u=\xi$ viewed as a unit and $P=$ `tateToricPoint ↥k₀ q (u^q)` (the toric point attached to $\xi^q$, of order $\ell_g$), one has $C.u\,(2P_1+6^{-1})=2P_2+P_1$, together with $C.r=-12^{-1}$, $C.s=-2^{-1}$, $C.t=24^{-1}$; (ii) the curve of $r$ maps, under $K\to k_0((t))$, to $C\cdot$ `tateBase ↥k₀ q`; (iii) for every prime factor $p$ of $M'$, every field $F'$ with a ring homomorphism $f:k_0\to F'$ and every primitive $p^{v_p(M')}$-th root of unity $\zeta\in F'$, the image of the $\Gamma_0$-kernel polynomial $r.\mathrm{level}_1(p)$ in $F'((t))$ equals the `kernelVariableChangeDeg` transform, by $f_*C$ in degree `gamma0PowDeg p (M'.factorization p)`, of $\prod_a (X-(\mathrm{toricPoint}\,F'\,q\,\zeta^a)_1)$, the product over $1\le a\le p^{v_p(M')}/2$ with $p\nmid a$; (iv) the image of the `LevelPData` component $r.\mathrm{level}_{2,1}$ is the variable-change transform by $C$ of the data $(P_1,P_2,P_1,P_2)$; (v) there exist $P_x,P_y,Q_x,Q_y\in K$ whose Laurent expansions are the four coordinates of the transform by $C$ of `cuspData ↥k₀ q (u^{ℓg}) ![1,0] ![0,-1]`, and the two Drinfeld sections of $r.\mathrm{level}_{2,2}$ pass through $(P_x,P_y)$ and $(Q_x,Q_y)$ respectively in the sense of `IsSectionThrough`.
--
--   Finally let $\theta:\kappa(A_0)\to\kappa(A)$ be a ring homomorphism compatible with the residue maps of $A_0$ and $A$ (`hθ`).
--
--   **Conclusion.** Under these hypotheses the following holds. Let $y$ be a maximal ideal of the chart algebra `chartAlgFin A₀ K j` and let $\psi$ be an $A_0$-algebra homomorphism from that chart algebra to $\kappa(A_0)$ whose zero set is exactly $y$. Let $x$ be a raw $\mathcal R$-datum over $\kappa(A_0)$ whose class in $\mathcal R.\mathrm{Pt}(\kappa(A_0))$ is the image of the universal point $P_0.\mathrm{univ}$ under $\psi\circ\mathrm{clC}$. Assume that the curve of $x$ has no non-trivial $q$-torsion over $\kappa(A_0)$: every point $P$ with $q\cdot P=0$ is zero. Let $g$ be a point of the affine curve of $x$ satisfying the hypothesis `hg`, namely that $g$ has exact additive order $M'$, and that for every prime factor $p$ of $M'$, every $n$, and every affine nonsingular pair $(x_1,y_1)$ with $n\cdot g=(x_1,y_1)$ and $n\cdot g$ of exact order $p^{v_p(M')}$, the point $x_1$ is a root of the $\Gamma_0$-kernel polynomial $x.\mathrm{level}_1(p)$. Let $r$ be a place of `modularFunctionFieldC (ResidueField A) M'` over $\kappa(A)$ which is rational and whose valuation subring contains `jGeomGen (ResidueField A) M'`. Assume that $r$ reads off the point $y$ in the following sense: for every $g_f$ in the full level-$M'$ modular function field `modularFunctionFieldFull M'` such that the image of $g_f$ in `modularFunctionFieldBar M'` is $R_0$-integral, such that this image has non-negative order at every place of `modularFunctionFieldBar M'` at which the image of `jq` has non-negative order, and such that `coeffEmb ↥k₀ g_f` lies in $K$ and in the chart algebra, the $R_0$-residue of $g_f$ lies in the valuation subring of $r$, and $\theta(\psi(g_f))$ equals the value $r.\mathrm{evalAt}$ of that residue.
--
--   Then there exists a place $r'$ of [`ModularCurve.modularFunctionFieldFullC (ResidueField A) M'`](def/ModularCurve_X0ModL.html#L100) over $\kappa(A)$ such that:
--
--   1.
--
--   the preimage of the valuation subring of $r'$ under the inclusion `modularFunctionFieldC (ResidueField A) M' ≤ modularFunctionFieldFullC (ResidueField A) M'` is the valuation subring of $r$; and
--
--   2.
--
--   $r'$ is a moduli place, in the sense of [`ModularCurve.IsModuliPlaceOf (ResidueField A) M'`](def/ModularCurve_ModuliPlace.html#L325), of the level-$M'$ moduli point obtained from the class of the $\Gamma_0(M')$-pair $(x.\mathrm{curve},\,g)$ over $\kappa(A_0)$ — the curve being elliptic because its discriminant is a unit, and $g$ of exact order $M'$ — by transporting it along the ring homomorphism $a\mapsto \theta(a)^q$, that is, $\theta$ followed by the $q$-power Frobenius of $\kappa(A)$. Explicitly, there are a field $\Omega$ over $\kappa(A)$ and a `ModuliTestDatum` $D$ for that moduli point over $\Omega$ with the valuation subring of $r'$ equal to the preimage of $D.W$'s valuation subring under the embedding $D.\mathrm{emb}$.
--
--   This is the step identifying, at a supersingular closed point of the rigid $H_1$-chart, the place of the level-$M'$ function field read off by the chart with a moduli place of the Frobenius twist of the transported $\Gamma_0(M')$-class; it is the geometric input for the special-fibre dictionary in characteristic $q$. It is used by [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.Diamond.exists_injective_forall_place_eq_of_forall_evalAt_eq_of_eq_map_classify_rigidDataH1Pow_of_tatePoint_pinGamma1`](thm.html#ModularCurve.FullLevel.Diamond.exists_injective_forall_place_eq_of_forall_evalAt_eq_of_eq_map_classify_rigidDataH1Pow_of_tatePoint_pinGamma1), the injectivity-of-places statement at the same level.
